/*  FUNCTION NAME:      MAZELAM_DIAG
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Stock Mazelam for MAZE: diagonal steps cost 1.5x the destination cell's Cost; cardinal steps cost 1x. Produces realistic Euclidean-ish distance over a uniform map.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array of step costs (numbers): 1.5x destination cost on diagonals, 1x on cardinals
    PARAMETERS:
        costFrom        (Required) Cost at the source cell. (Unused by this Mazelam.)
        costTo          (Required) Cost at the destination cell. Multiplied by 1.5 on diagonals.
        cellFrom        (Required) A1 address of source cell (e.g. "C3"). Use ROWNUM/COLNUM to decode.
        cellTo          (Required) A1 address of destination cell (e.g. "D4").
        distFrom        (Required) Cumulative cost to reach source. (Unused by this Mazelam.)
        dirDelta        (Required) This step's direction, encoded row*_mult+col. (Unused.)
        prevDir         (Required) Previous direction. (Unused.)
    EXAMPLE:            =MAZE("A1", myCosts, , , , , , MAZELAM_DIAG) -> Distance grid where diagonal moves cost 1.5x and cardinals cost 1x
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-05-20  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-05-27  Claude      Signature changed: cellFrom/cellTo (A1 strings) replace rowFrom/colFrom/rowTo/colTo
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
MAZELAM_DIAG = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [costFrom],
    [costTo],
    [cellFrom],
    [cellTo],
    [distFrom],
    [dirDelta],
    [prevDir],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        diagonal, (ROWNUM(cellFrom) <> ROWNUM(cellTo)) * (COLNUM(cellFrom) <> COLNUM(cellTo)),
        result, IF(diagonal = 1, costTo * 1.5, costTo),
        result
)
);
